      "score": 94,
      "summary": "B gives every finding evidence, runtime unknowns, concrete repairs and its own acceptance criteria. Hostile-data and failure coverage is the strongest of the three, with truthful save recovery and upload replacement safety. Its provisional performance table covers latency, long tasks, mounted rows, CLS, memory and base-to-head regression limits, and it gives explicit rollback and safe-fallback rules. It keeps scale at P1 unless runtime evidence shows otherwise, which is careful about evidence. Scope stays disciplined."
    },
