      "score": 90,
      "summary": "A is thorough and honest. It has a clear failure matrix, careful evidence-versus-hypothesis labeling, and the best decisive-versus-contextual reconciliation, which also preserves existing foundations. Its performance gates are proposed and calibrated against a baseline, but they are less complete than B's: no row cap, memory or regression thresholds. Acceptance conditions are grouped in the validation plan rather than attached to each fix."
